<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.10" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="18776-5" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Plan of care note"/>
    <title>Plan of Treatment</title>
    <text><list><item>Stop reliever-only albuterol and start budesonide-formoterol maintenance-and-reliever therapy at Step 4 (two inhalations twice daily plus one as needed, up to 12 a day), with a spacer and inhaler-technique teaching. Guideline: Global Strategy for Asthma Management and Prevention, 2025 update (2025); 2020 Focused Updates to the Asthma Management Guidelines: A Report from the National Asthma Education and Prevention Program Coordinating Committee Expert Panel Working Group (2020) [S]</item><item>Written asthma action plan with symptom and peak-flow zones (green 80 percent or more of personal best, yellow 50 to 79 percent, red below 50 percent), reviewed at every visit and after every exacerbation. Guideline: Global Strategy for Asthma Management and Prevention, 2025 update (2025); 2020 Focused Updates to the Asthma Management Guidelines: A Report from the National Asthma Education and Prevention Program Coordinating Committee Expert Panel Working Group (2020); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, asthma monograph (2026) [S]</item><item>Pulmonology referral to confirm the diagnosis, assess type 2 inflammation, and advise on exercise-induced symptoms, allergen measures, and treatment step. Guideline: Global Strategy for Asthma Management and Prevention, 2025 update (2025); 2020 Focused Updates to the Asthma Management Guidelines: A Report from the National Asthma Education and Prevention Program Coordinating Committee Expert Panel Working Group (2020) [S]</item><item>Asthma Control Test, inhaler technique, adherence, reliever use, triggers, and exacerbation history at every visit; review one to three months after starting controller therapy, then every three to twelve months, and within one week of any exacerbation; spirometry at diagnosis, three to six months after stabilization, then every one to two years. Guideline: Global Strategy for Asthma Management and Prevention, 2025 update (2025); 2020 Focused Updates to the Asthma Management Guidelines: A Report from the National Asthma Education and Prevention Program Coordinating Committee Expert Panel Working Group (2020); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, asthma monograph (2026) [S]</item><item>Explain that exercise improves fitness but does not treat airway inflammation; take one reliever inhalation before boxing or rowing; use dust-mite-impermeable bedding covers once sensitization is shown. Guideline: Global Strategy for Asthma Management and Prevention, 2025 update (2025); 2020 Focused Updates to the Asthma Management Guidelines: A Report from the National Asthma Education and Prevention Program Coordinating Committee Expert Panel Working Group (2020) [S]</item><item>Yearly influenza vaccine, pneumococcal vaccination for chronic lung disease, and COVID-19 vaccination by CDC guidance. Guideline: CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, asthma monograph (2026); Summary of Risk-based Pneumococcal Vaccination Recommendations (2025) [S]</item></list></text>

  </section>
